## What I found

The dsh-migrate pipeline did rename the vocabulary and the plugin now cold-boots on 0.1.2-alpha.2, but the final artifact **fails the statement's route acceptance test** and is not the mandated minimal rename:

| Check | Pipeline artifact | Minimal rename (comparison copy) |
|---|---|---|
| Old names fail `pending (tasks, httpServer)` | baseline: PASS | — |
| Web-profile boot, no pending entry | PASS | PASS |
| **plain `GET /bench-status/status`** | **401 `unauthorized`** (404 without a `connection` service) | **200 `{"ok":true,"open":0}`** |

Root cause: the pipeline's review treated the whole rc.1→alpha.2 corridor as in scope, applied security card `DSH-0.1.2-A1-08` (Connection gate), and then its headless boot-check forced the `webServer`/`connection` injection to be scoped — so it shipped `inject: ['jobs']` + `ctx.inject(['webServer','connection'])` instead of the required `inject: ['jobs','webServer']` rename. Its passing boot check uses a base/headless probe profile (no web carrier), the web/e2e checks were skipped, and its claimed 401/200 web validation was run against `/tmp/plugin-src-copy`, a pre-repair copy — the final artifact was never web-tested or re-reviewed (`repair-1.md` is just a 2-line error dump). The pipeline also kept **no `cards.json`** (cards check skipped: "no source release is known"), so the report cites the applicable cards from the skill corridor: `DSH-0.1.1-R1-09` (required, partially honored), `DSH-0.1.1-R1-04`, `DSH-0.1.1-R1-05`, `DSH-0.1.2-A1-08`, `DSH-0.1.2-A2-03`.

